{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix","id":1531844,"title":"shadow Flesh legacy/Strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-02T07:58:34-08:00","id":1531844,"title":"shadow Flesh legacy/Strix","content":"So, I happen to like the Strix rather a lot, great piece of storytelling equipment for any Requiem game.<br /> <br /> But also I dislike the &quot;they are actually human spirits, or whatever happened to human spirits...&quot;<br /> <br /> So what if a Mage (Thyrsus) gets this idea of human spirits and the Strix, and in exploring and learning Death makes a legacy with Shadow Flesh as the capstone.<br /> <br /> Now the Spirit master has a plan, to explore Dis (in shadow form) and hopefully find the truth ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":"fixing typo) 03-02-2024, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T08:41:48-08:00","id":1531845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix#post1531844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I happen to like the Strix rather a lot, great piece of storytelling equipment for any Requiem game.<br /> <br /> But also I dislike the &quot;they are actually human spirits, or whatever happened to human spirits...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The events <i>HIJACK: The Writer's Guide to the Strix</i> attributes to the departure of humanity from the Strix are so far back in the history of the real world that they pre-date the earliest point on <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>'s timeline that hasn't been erased from history by an order of magnitude, and that itself pre-dates the Sundering by an order of magnitude.<br /> <br /> <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> describes the &quot;root peoples&quot; in terms that make it plain that weird spiritual phenomena relating to human prehistory are far from unheard of, and <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> likewise reiterates (by way of remnant Neanderthal populations) the reoccurring notion that spending long enough in the Shadow can turn a creature into a spirit. On the other end of the age gap, their weird relationship with time notwithstanding, the immortality-granting alien beings known as the Visitors have emerged/spawned at least as recently as the Trinity nuclear tests, where they were created as part of the event's impact on local spirits.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that it's not exactly a wild or diminutive theory to have traction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what if a Mage (Thyrsus) gets this idea of human spirits and the Strix, and in exploring and learning Death makes a legacy with Shadow Flesh as the capstone.<br /> <br /> Now the Spirit master has a plan, to explore Dis (in shadow form) and hopefully find the truth ... </div> </div> </div>What we know about the Lower Depths and the Dark Places both establish that, unless you have a plot device for making it back to Earth, this is functionally an elaborate form of suicide to attempt for longer than a scene. Is the idea that this is part of a Threshold Seeking or did you have another method in mind for making this relevant beyond &quot;a powerful mage wants to enter a place none return from&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T13:27:15-08:00","id":1531852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531845#post1531845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The events <i>HIJACK: The Writer's Guide to the Strix</i> attributes to the departure of humanity from the Strix are so far back in the history of the real world that they pre-date the earliest point on <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>'s timeline that hasn't been erased from history by an order of magnitude, and that itself pre-dates the Sundering by an order of magnitude.<br /> <br /> <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> describes the &quot;root peoples&quot; in terms that make it plain that weird spiritual phenomena relating to human prehistory are far from unheard of, and <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> likewise reiterates (by way of remnant Neanderthal populations) the reoccurring notion that spending long enough in the Shadow can turn a creature into a spirit. On the other end of the age gap, their weird relationship with time notwithstanding, the immortality-granting alien beings known as the Visitors have emerged/spawned at least as recently as the Trinity nuclear tests, where they were created as part of the event's impact on local spirits.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that it's not exactly a wild or diminutive theory to have traction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am missing your point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What we know about the Lower Depths and the Dark Places both establish that, unless you have a plot device for making it back to Earth, this is functionally an elaborate form of suicide to attempt for longer than a scene. Is the idea that this is part of a Threshold Seeking or did you have another method in mind for making this relevant beyond &quot;a powerful mage wants to enter a place none return from&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I think it is an interesting plot point. Whether they can possibly return or not would he unknown.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a powerful NPC, maybe the players discover them after they have dissapeared and have to decide what to do with the notes/daimonokon.<br /> <br /> Do they attempt to rescue someone from Dis? Destroy all record of the Legacy to avoid anyone else dying?<br /> <br /> If anyone can survive in Dis, I think a creature of shadow has a chance. Doing so by shaping your soul rather than drawing on the Supernal seems much safer (since you can probably bring your soul with you, it maybe more difficult to draw upon your path).<br /> <br /> And especially a Mage who has studied the creatures which apparently emanate from Dis. Time spent with a Strix under Focused Mage Sight might offer insights which would make survival more likely - even if this remains a one way trip.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what else I had in mind, a threshold seeking could be interesting, but I would rather if there was a metaphysical reason for any archmage Shenanigans to end up affecting the deep past rather than the future, what does Dis lack? If this shadow Mage achieved Archmastery while in Dis, even if they were still trapped there (might be even more incentive for players to try rescuing her) would they be able to perform serious world altering magic to either return or change the nature of the Strix (comparable to whatever made them not spirit shadow entities effectively banished from both the material and spirit worlds?)<br /> <br /> Ok, maybe an Archmaster trapped in Dis actually trying to get people to A) join his legacy and B) help create the quintessense needed to get back from Dis, would be even more difficult for players to resolve...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T14:50:40-08:00","id":1531853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix#post1531844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I happen to like the Strix rather a lot, great piece of storytelling equipment for any Requiem game.<br /> <br /> But also I dislike the &quot;they are actually human spirits, or whatever happened to human spirits...&quot;<br /> <br /> So what if a Mage (Thyrsus) gets this idea of human spirits and the Strix, and in exploring and learning Death makes a legacy with Shadow Flesh as the capstone.<br /> <br /> Now the Spirit master has a plan, to explore Dis (in shadow form) and hopefully find the truth ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to ask, but what's the connection between disliking the Hijack stuff and your story idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T15:09:20-08:00","id":1531854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531852#post1531852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am missing your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without having been provided a reason for disliking the origin of the Strix put forth in Rose Bailey's Storyteller's Vault product about them, I am presenting reasons why that origin doesn't lock down or limit them in any substantial fashion that would make it necessary to contextualize a comparatively straightforward &quot;What if a Legacy Master tried to explore one of the Lower Depths?&quot; hypothetical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe this is a powerful NPC, maybe the players discover them after they have dissapeared and have to decide what to do with the notes/daimonokon.<br /> <br /> Do they attempt to rescue someone from Dis? Destroy all record of the Legacy to avoid anyone else dying? </div> </div> </div>I should think annotating the notes and turning them over to the Mysterium or the Guardians (depending on how novel the Legacy is and what its theory and consequences are) would suffice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anyone can survive in Dis, I think a creature of shadow has a chance. Doing so by shaping your soul rather than drawing on the Supernal seems much safer (since you can probably bring your soul with you, it maybe more difficult to draw upon your path). </div> </div> </div>I am opting to discount the explicit statement that the things capable of entering the Dark Places are specifically those with a connection to vampirism, but the issue is much more plainly &quot;Only the most powerful Strix can open a gateway to this place in complete darkness and some of them do so for a reason couched in language that would equate to a form of death,&quot; i.e. even if you were to treat &quot;Dis&quot; like a conventional otherworld, it's still one for which you have no way to ensure an exit will show up close enough for you to reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And especially a Mage who has studied the creatures which apparently emanate from Dis. Time spent with a Strix under Focused Mage Sight might offer insights which would make survival more likely - even if this remains a one way trip. </div> </div> </div>The Strix are uncommon enough and covert enough that much of vampiric society isn't convinced they exist, the overwhelming majority of them are native to the material world, as a phenomenon they're like Kindred vampires in terms of being a bunch of different things similar enough to share game mechanics, and where &quot;Dis&quot; may be assumed to be a singular place conventionally thought equates it with a Lower Depth for all the reasons you'd expect.<br /> <br /> Story hooks are nice, but past a certain point one has to acknowledge that the number of variables that need to align to facilitate a given conclusion is nontrivial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not sure what else I had in mind, a threshold seeking could be interesting, but I would rather if there was a metaphysical reason for any archmage Shenanigans to end up affecting the deep past rather than the future, </div> </div> </div>Aponoia. Aponoia is practically part and parcel of &quot;archmage shenanigans.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what does Dis lack? </div> </div> </div>Vitae, as per the conventional wisdom of the Depths, for all that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454571#post1454571\">that's only really a useful descriptor in the most oversimplified terms</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this shadow Mage achieved Archmastery while in Dis, even if they were still trapped there (might be even more incentive for players to try rescuing her) </div> </div> </div>Without invoking a plot device that isn't published in any of the books, the only way an archmaster can be objectively trapped in a place (rather than not wanting to leave for personal reasons) is through Imperial Paradox on a spell powerful enough to create a subsoul or a Chantry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> would they be able to perform serious world altering magic to either return or change the nature of the Strix (comparable to whatever made them not spirit shadow entities effectively banished from both the material and spirit worlds?) </div> </div> </div>The main things that can prevent an archmaster from performing serious world-altering magic would be, again, Imperial Paradox cutting them off from the Golden Road that allows them to channel Quintessence and perform Imperium Rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, maybe an Archmaster trapped in Dis actually trying to get people to A) join his legacy and B) help create the quintessense needed to get back from Dis, would be even more difficult for players to resolve... </div> </div> </div>Why does the character want people to join his Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T15:40:51-08:00","id":1531856,"title":"","content":"What is their methodology for investigating the Stryx ? Since its a Mystery worthy of crafting an entire Legacy around, what kind of power or insight do they expect to harness ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T11:02:53-08:00","id":1531904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531854#post1531854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without having been provided a reason for disliking the origin of the Strix put forth in Rose Bailey's Storyteller's Vault product about them, I am presenting reasons why that origin doesn't lock down or limit them in any substantial fashion that would make it necessary to contextualize a comparatively straightforward &quot;What if a Legacy Master tried to explore one of the Lower Depths?&quot; hypothetical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that context does help actually, reading some of the Tome stuff is interesting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should think annotating the notes and turning them over to the Mysterium or the Guardians (depending on how novel the Legacy is and what its theory and consequences are) would suffice. </div> </div> </div>I would hope to find players who are more proactive...I mean, those are all valid decisions, but also feel like ignore the question and let someone else handle it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am opting to discount the explicit statement that the things capable of entering the Dark Places are specifically those with a connection to vampirism </div> </div> </div>Where is this particular piece written? I think sufficient study of the Strix and Patterning magic should fit the requirement, but ::shrugs::<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , but the issue is much more plainly &quot;Only the most powerful Strix can open a gateway to this place in complete darkness and some of them do so for a reason couched in language that would equate to a form of death,&quot; i.e. even if you were to treat &quot;Dis&quot; like a conventional otherworld, it's still one for which you have no way to ensure an exit will show up close enough for you to reach. </div> </div> </div>There are legacies that gain access to specific Emanation realms, so it would not be unprecedented to have a specific connection to access Dis...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Strix are uncommon enough and covert enough that much of vampiric society isn't convinced they exist, the overwhelming majority of them are native to the material world, as a phenomenon they're like Kindred vampires in terms of being a bunch of different things similar enough to share game mechanics, and where &quot;Dis&quot; may be assumed to be a singular place conventionally thought equates it with a Lower Depth for all the reasons you'd expect. </div> </div> </div>If anyone already has basic backgrounds und information on them, it is likely to Mages, and if anyone has the capacity to find and rlstudy them, again this is where Mage's strength lies.<br /> <br /> Whether that is done by negotiation, or less salubrious methods...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Story hooks are nice, but past a certain point one has to acknowledge that the number of variables that need to align to facilitate a given conclusion is nontrivial. </div> </div> </div>Again, in all the history of the Pentacle at least one Mage must have written something about them, whether as rumour or prophecy or lies told them by a Strix they met.<br /> <br /> That combined with Mages are great at investigating things...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aponoia. Aponoia is practically part and parcel of &quot;archmage shenanigans.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vitae, as per the conventional wisdom of the Depths, for all that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454571#post1454571\">that's only really a useful descriptor in the most oversimplified terms</a>. </div> </div> </div>Hmm, Vitae is somehow related to Life and Death, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without invoking a plot device that isn't published in any of the books, the only way an archmaster can be objectively trapped in a place (rather than not wanting to leave for personal reasons) is through Imperial Paradox on a spell powerful enough to create a subsoul or a Chantry.<br /> <br /> The main things that can prevent an archmaster from performing serious world-altering magic would be, again, Imperial Paradox cutting them off from the Golden Road that allows them to channel Quintessence and perform Imperium Rites. </div> </div> </div>Maybe forging the Archmastery for now, a Master who needs to gain Archmastery to escape would be interesting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does the character want people to join his Legacy? </div> </div> </div>Alternatively this may be a bit of a b'ait and switch.<br /> <br /> You can only leave this lower depth is you swap yourself out with someone else... Maybe joining the legacy is a step towards being kidnapped...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531853#post1531853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry to ask, but what's the connection between disliking the Hijack stuff and your story idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just background to what has me thinking about it.<br /> <br /> Using the idea of Strix as human spirits to create something interesting gameplay/story rather than abstract metaphysics... And of course Mage is probably the most capable splatt of exploring that.<br /> <br /> Though if you have suggestions of who else would be interested in such a project, please share your ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531856#post1531856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is their methodology for investigating the Stryx ? Since its a Mystery worthy of crafting an entire Legacy around, what kind of power or insight do they expect to harness ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that this seems to be back story for an NPC at this point, magic?<br /> <br /> Or more specificly Fate to find them and Death sight to study the shadows....<br /> <br /> Maybe Life and Death to get deeper. Given their powers and control of Vitae are similar to vampires.<br /> <br /> Insight into their nature, the Strix seem to act like Changelings (from star trek) in that they reproduce by splitting off into two individuals, so this part of their nature might be interesting. Then there is their ability to possess and even seemingly become one with their host, not unlike other ephemerals in a sense, but it feels deeper, like they create kindred if they wish (but may give up themselves to do so? Mechanically the rules are unclear).<br /> <br /> But I prefer the idea that a Mage obsessed with finding the truth of their past, home, and relationship to humans (as opposed to kindred).\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T14:57:55-08:00","id":1531925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1531904#post1531904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hope to find players who are more proactive...I mean, those are all valid decisions, but also feel like ignore the question and let someone else handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A person we've never met before started a Legacy concerning a place we've never heard of and then disappeared&quot; would seem to be a question with no inherent hook to it, unless the Master in question had something else the PCs need or want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this particular piece written? I think sufficient study of the Strix and Patterning magic should fit the requirement, but ::shrugs:: </div> </div> </div>In the Dark Places Embodiment in Vampire 2e Core. &quot;Anything with a taint of the Strix\u2019s nature \u2014 Strix, vampires, and ghouls, for example \u2014 may cross over to the Strix\u2019s world entirely by spending a Willpower point. The gateway only stays open for a scene, however, and anyone seeking the ancient Strix must cross back over in time or be lost.&quot; Sufficient study was why I said I was opting to discount that particular element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are legacies that gain access to specific Emanation realms, so it would not be unprecedented to have a specific connection to access Dis... </div> </div> </div>Emanation Realms are easier to learn about through Mage Sight than most other dimensions because they're Supernal phenomena. Dis is a Lower Depth that requires a Strix with Shadow Potency 10 to access for a scene in complete darkness. The two are not the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anyone already has basic backgrounds und information on them, it is likely to Mages, and if anyone has the capacity to find and rlstudy them, again this is where Mage's strength lies.<br /> <br /> Whether that is done by negotiation, or less salubrious methods...<br /> <br /> Again, in all the history of the Pentacle at least one Mage must have written something about them, whether as rumour or prophecy or lies told them by a Strix they met.<br /> <br /> That combined with Mages are great at investigating things... </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages&quot; does not translate to &quot;any mage&quot; and &quot;the information exists&quot; does not translate to &quot;a mage has access to that information.&quot; Mage Sight gives particular categories of information and the rest requires legwork and relevant spells. Dealing with the Lower Depths is rightly looked upon with suspicion by conventional Awakened society. Records of obscure knowledge come from somewhere, and that obscurity tends to lend weight to the names of the people who went to the trouble of finding it, particularly among people as prideful as mages.<br /> <br /> Again, we're talking about the bogeymen of a more accessible supernatural culture that have naturalized themselves into the material world and sprung forth from a variety of sources, which <i>may</i> be able to access a realm of primordial darkness at the height of their power in conditions that preclude visually-oriented beings from seeing it do so. You can't handwave that with &quot;mages are good at finding stuff out,&quot; least of all when the stuff in question relates to a Lower Depth and one of the mysteries of the human soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, Vitae is somehow related to Life and Death, right? </div> </div> </div>Yup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T03:18:23-08:00","id":1531947,"title":"","content":"All the Mysteries that are worth solving require legwork...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:49:11-08:00","id":1532035,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you could make them specialized in dealing with Stryx and capturing them. The legend of the Stryx is linked to witches, so the Thyrsus Path works out well. Perhaps Death and Spirit, which would allow for abilities like making a modified soul jar to capture them (think the ghost trap from <i>Ghostbusters</i>) and eventually allow them to develop a transformation that grants them Stryx like abilities (which would become the gateway to entering and returning from Dis). If humans are connected to the Stryx in some manner, then the potential to harness their power exists within the human soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T03:14:06-08:00","id":1532074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531844-shadow-flesh-legacy-strix?p=1532035#post1532035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps you could make them specialized in dealing with Stryx and capturing them. The legend of the Stryx is linked to witches, so the Thyrsus Path works out well. Perhaps Death and Spirit, which would allow for abilities like making a modified soul jar to capture them (think the ghost trap from <i>Ghostbusters</i>) and eventually allow them to develop a transformation that grants them Stryx like abilities (which would become the gateway to entering and returning from Dis). If humans are connected to the Stryx in some manner, then the potential to harness their power exists within the human soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Harnessing the Strix's power is what turning a human into a vampire looks like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, capturing them is one option, one of the things I like about the Strix is that they seem inclined to make deals (terrible option for most folks) they are associated with bringing* Doom, right?<br /> <br /> I see the potential for a Mage deciding that they can cure quiescense by re-integeating the Strix into the human soul, like the spark of the Abyss is a flaw, and you could theories that the absence of human spirits/Strix like entity is what causes it...<br /> <br /> Negotiations rather than capture seems like a lot of fun. I mean, also potentially more likely to end up being labelled as left-handed, but fun!<br /> <br /> *Or at least being followed by it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}